        "title": "Expert Backed Review Summary",
        "text": "<p>Kinoko Platinum centers on <strong>AHCC®</strong>, a proprietary cultured extract derived from mushroom mycelia, including <em>Lentinula edodes</em>. Each vegetarian capsule contains 750 mg, while the labeled two-capsule serving provides 1.5 g. AHCC has been investigated in human studies for its effects on immune responses, including natural killer, T-cell, macrophage and dendritic-cell activity. However, these findings should be viewed as supportive research rather than evidence that the supplement prevents or treats disease. The concentrated 750 mg capsules make reaching the manufacturer's 1.5–3 g daily range relatively straightforward. The formula is vegetarian, gluten-free, dairy-free and GMO-free, with 60 capsules providing 30 servings at the standard two-capsule serving size. It's a focused option for users specifically interested in AHCC, but anyone managing a medical condition, taking medication, or using it alongside treatment should discuss supplementation with a healthcare professional. </p><h3></h3>",
